<title>PAKISTAN: PAKISTAN MONEY RATES END UP ON FUND SHORTAGE.</title>
<headline>PAKISTAN MONEY RATES END UP ON FUND SHORTAGE.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's money market rates ended up on Monday owing to a shortage of funds and are likely to stay firm on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The overnight rates traded in the range of 14 and 17.50 percent owing to the shortage of funds,&quot; said a dealer at Standard Chartered Bank. &quot;Early deals were struck at levels around 15 percent, but towards the close they shot up to 17.50 percent.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Amir Zia (9221) 5685192; Fax 5673428</p>
